text.en:
Before submitting, the platform may show one of three alerts:
• a known outage right now;
• the service you're asking about is affected;
• you already have a similar open ticket.

If the alert matches your issue, you don't need a new ticket — follow the open one or the status page. If it's different, submit as usual.

This panel gathers what needs action from you, each item with a button to the right place. The common ones:
• tickets awaiting your reply;
• a plan or WhatsApp subscription about to expire;
• low or empty WhatsApp balance;
• smart-assistant messages nearly used up;
• an announced outage or a degraded service;
• adding a phone number or turning on two-step verification.

When everything is fine, the panel says your account is healthy.

Under "Usage & limits" in the sidebar:
• your plans and subscriptions with their end dates;
• WhatsApp balance and its last 5 transactions;
• smart-assistant messages used from your quota.

That section is read-only; top-ups and upgrades happen from "Plans & subscription" or through support.

The proof file can be at most 8MB. If it's larger:
• take a screenshot of the receipt instead of a camera photo — much smaller;
• or save it as PDF from your banking app;
• or resize the image on your phone (Share → medium size).

The amount, date and transaction number must stay readable.

If the bot replies that "this code isn't right or has expired":
• codes are single-use and time-limited — request a new one from the settings page;
• send it alone in a message, with no spaces or text before it;
• make sure you're sending it to the right bot.

If it replies "a temporary problem occurred", that's on our side — wait a minute and try again.

If the assistant isn't replying, the usual reasons are:
• the assistant message quota is used up, or access expired — you'll see an alert in the account-health panel;
• on Telegram: the account isn't linked yet — send the link code first;
• the assistant is temporarily switched off in the team's settings.

In every case regular support still works: open a ticket from "My tickets".

Security notifications concern something sensitive on your account. Open it and see what it's about:
• if it's something you did (like changing your password), nothing is needed;
• if not: change your password now, turn on two-step verification, and tell me so I can open a security ticket.

A link preview (image and title) is built from the page's own metadata, and won't show when:
• the page has no preview image and title (og:image, og:title);
• the link is shortened or redirects several times;
• the link is glued to other text.

The message itself is delivered normally even without a preview.
